  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 1404.02 Specification Used Oil",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 1404.02 Specification Used Oil.\n\n(a) Used oil shall be classified as specification used oil if the oil:\n\n(1) Has not been mixed with any other hazardous waste; and\n\n(2) Meets all of the allowable levels in Table 14.1 below:\n\nTable 14.1 Specification Used Oil Standards\n\nConstituent/Property | Allowable Level\n\nArsenic | 5 ppm maximum\n\nCadmium | 2 ppm maximum\n\nChromium | 10 ppm maximum\n\nLead | 100 ppm maximum\n\nFlash point | 100 degrees Fahrenheit minimum\n\nPolychlorinated biphenyls (PCBs) | Less than 2 ppm\n\nTotal halogens | 1,000 ppm maximum\n\n(b) Except as specified in Env-Hw 1402.03(b), the standards in Table 14.1 do not apply to mixtures of used oil and hazardous waste.\n\nSource. #14282, eff 8-1-25, EXPIRES: 8-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html"
}
